  "method": "Each pinned day of LANL host logs is read line by line; events whose EventID one of the Windows rules names become rows with Windows EventData field names (logs.py, lanl_row). Every rule is compiled by pySigma-backend-sqlite and run on the week an hour at a time, with the longest correlation window before each hour also loaded. A correlation alert is a run of overlapping qualifying windows for one group; a single-event alert is one matching event. LANL doesn't label the data, so every alert counts as a false alarm.",
